  "summary_en": "Grunge Mold Spots generates a pattern of layered noise that looks like mold spots. It can be used as a mask or as a building block for detailed textures, such as fungus-stained surfaces.",
  "inputs": [
    "size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Range: Amplitude, Center, Mask Contrast",
    "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale (with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size",
    "Spread: blurs the spots; higher values cover more area, lower values sharpen them",
    "Primary Size, Secondary Size, Tertiary Size: size of each spot layer relative to Element Size; larger values give fewer, bigger spots",
    "Secondary Mask and Tertiary Mask: visibility of those layers",
    "Seed: changes the randomization while keeping the same look",
    "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Output can be negative or above 1; use Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum",
    "Fold has no effect when all values are positive",
    "Complement produces valid results only for values from 0 to 1",
    "Post-processing Contrast differs from Noise Contrast"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Grunge Mold Spots produit un motif de taches de moisissure par bruits superposés, utilisable en masque ou pour des surfaces tachées de champignons."
